!! Vitals

* ''Branch'' `feature/lararium-node-5`, ahead of `origin` — `git rev-list --count origin/feature/lararium-node-5..HEAD` reads the unpushed commits; the operator pushes. Working tree clean apart from crew-held paths: `mempalace` (submodule), `tests/harness/instance.ts`, untracked `tests/e2e/nexus-offering-replication.test.ts`, `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/`, `.worktrees/`. Never commit, stash, or revert those.
* ''Corpus'': every tracked `bags/*.mem` reads canonical under `lares meme check`; `tools/bcc-witness.sh` reads every block check `ok`; the submissions shelf (`bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/submissions/`) reads 6 pairs, 0 out of step.
* ''The witness fleet'' (`tools/witness-all.sh`, what CI runs) ends on a verdict table, one line per witness with its own exit code — count the reds there, never in the transcript. Three read red: `contract-witness` ("A's members board folds B IN" — see `#/wounds` P1, the presented-admit gate), `vessel-parity-witness` (`makePersonaGroupIdentityRing` composes on node only — the browser side is owed), `typecheck-witness` (the two crew reds, `packages/lararium-web/src/main.ts:98` and `tests/harness/scenario-action-graph.ts:175`). Every other witness reads ok; `symbol-anchor-witness` holds at its ceiling of 37, and `hearths-gate-witness` derives its second-hearth probe from the live holds. Each dist-reading witness refuses a stale build by name — rebuild the named package, run `node tools/stamp-build.mjs`, re-run.
* ''CI'' (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) validates; the `VSCode-TW5-Syntax` pin `d2d17eeb9` stands on that submodule's remote at `release/3.0.0`, so checkout resolves. The build, test, witness and e2e jobs have not yet run past checkout — the next push or a re-run of the failed run is their first real witness. `.github/workflows/held-out.yml` fails validation on every push at 0s — a job-level `env:` reads `runner.temp`, which that scope does not offer; the file sits on the Codex hearth's hold, and the fix waits for that crew in `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/handback-eot2-and-typecheck-reds` `#/held-out-workflow`.
* ''The tree is shared'': a parallel lane edits `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/wsl2/**` and `tools/wsl2/**` and re-stamps after editing — a witness run mid-edit reads its carriers as drifted for a minute. Re-run before believing a red there.
* ''Typecheck'' (`tools/typecheck-witness.sh`): two reds, both crew-held — `packages/lararium-web/src/main.ts:98` and `tests/harness/scenario-action-graph.ts:175`.
* ''Every package builds'' from clean (`pnpm -r build`).
* ''Known test reds'' and their owners:
** `lararium-node` `tests/bind-under-handle.test.ts` — crew: the joinee boot path never supplies `expectedEpoch` (the binding gate needs the live lease epoch, as `face-join.ts` supplies it); never revert the gate.
** `lares-cli` `tests/help-door-meme.test.ts`, `tests/nexus-verb-reach.test.ts` — crew: `nexus offering` keeps its help text outside the command registry.
** `lararium-tw5` `tests/syncer-back-parity.e2e.test.ts` (Chromium legs) and `tests/meme-routes.e2e.test.ts` — environmental (browser / server sockets).
** `lararium-tw5` corpus suites can fail on `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/wsl2/*.mem` while that lane edits them — its owner's to settle.
** `lararium-tw5` `tests/grammar-in-a-wiki.test.ts` — a corpus-wide walk that times out at the default 5 s under load; passes alone.

